<div class="rd-principles-strip">
    <div class="rd-principles-strip-inner">
        <h2>The core principles</h2>
        <div class="rd-principles-grid">
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Immediate results</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">Trust has to be rebuilt. People need to feel the benefit in order to believe in the plan.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Go with the grain</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">Good systems redirect human nature rather than suppress it. Price incentives beat moralising.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Give and take</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">A new social contract. Some big asks, but with lots in return. Fair and honest taxation.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Tax wealth, not work</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">The first £25k you earn is tax-free. Accumulated wealth, especially idle assets, pays its share.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Housing is the keystone</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">Pull it out and everything else follows. Land banking must cost money. Living must cost less.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="rd-principle">
                <div class="rd-principle-title">Iterate and evolve</div>
                <p class="rd-principle-desc">Economies are complex and no plan is perfect. So we monitor and adjust often.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
